From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 13:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Read device paths from /etc/nyx.conf at runtime

The touchscreen node and the power-supply sysfs paths were compile-time
-D defines, set by a per-machine cmake include. That is why this package
is PACKAGE_ARCH = MACHINE_ARCH and why there are 57 machine cmake files,
37 of which exist only to carry these paths.

They do not need to be built in. luneos-device-config already derives
the touchscreen at boot - exactly one input device advertises
ID_INPUT_TOUCHSCREEN, so no per-device knowledge is involved - and takes
anything genuinely underivable from the adaptation's deviceinfo. It
writes /etc/nyx.conf and bind-mounts it over the shipped default, so the
rootfs is never modified. The keys module has read [module.keys] paths=
this way for a while; this extends the same mechanism to the rest.

Precedence is runtime config, then the compile-time define, then the
existing detection, so nothing changes for a machine still built with
the defines and nothing changes on a device where the file is absent.

Groups and keys:

    [module.touchpanel] path
    [module.battery]    sysfs_path
    [module.charger]    usb_sysfs_path, ac_sysfs_path

An absent or empty value falls through, which is what lets the shipped
default declare the keys empty and leave detection in charge.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LuneOS-specific runtime configuration]
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
diff -urN a/include/internal/nyx_conf.h b/include/internal/nyx_conf.h
--- a/include/internal/nyx_conf.h	1970-01-01 01:00:00.000000000 +0100
+++ b/include/internal/nyx_conf.h	2026-08-24 13:44:00.629710044 +0200
@@ -0,0 +1,62 @@
